            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "shan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "love this recipe, but if you leave this on the grill for 20 minutes you will get mushy veggies.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-16T14:44:20.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jason Pierce"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The units of measure for pepper and garlic are clearly wrong. I used 2 tsp instead of 2 tbsp of black pepper. I also changed garlic to tsp instead of tbsp. Borderline inedible because of overpowering pepper and garlic. Ate a helping with my steak and tossed the rest.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-25T23:55:11.397Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Megan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dish was a huge hit with my son but there was way too much butter. Next time I will only use 1/4-1/3 cup. Serve with fresh parmesan cheese grated on top!",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-12T01:12:28.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I never use all that butter - it's way too much. I use I can't believe it's not butter spray. I add some fresh portabella mushrooms and some cherry tomatoes cut in half along with red onion cut into rings and a few dashes of italian seasoning. Also, the measurements for the salt and pepper may be a little off on here too. Just add to taste.",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-06T14:19:55.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "aly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We make these all the time. I could eat squash with every meal. Instead of the butter we use light olive oil. Also, we don't put the squash in foil, we cut them in thick slices and just stick them right on the grill. I find that the foil steams them too much and they become a bit soggy. I like my veggies to still have a crunch!",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-02T06:09:53.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
